: "text", "text": "(ii A.D.); cf. infr. c."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "2", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ". σύν AS ADV., together, at once,"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "κενεὰς ς. Χεῖρας ἔχοντες Od. 10.42", "author_abbreviation": "Od.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; mostly folld. by δέ or τε"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": ", ς. δὲ πτερὰ πυκνὰ λίασθεν Il. 23.879", "author_abbreviation": "Il.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ";"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ς. τε δύ' ἐρχομένω 10.224", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(cf. σύνδυο)"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "; ξ. τε διπλοῖ βασιλῆς S. Aj. 960", "author_abbreviation": "S.", "tlg_author": "0011", "tlg_work": "003", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(lyr.). It is sts. hard to distinguish this from tmesis, e.g. in"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Il. 23.879", "author_abbreviation": "Il.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; so ξὺν κακῶς ποιεῖν is = Ξυγκακοποιεῖν in"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Th. 3.13", "author_abbreviation": "Th.", "tlg_author": "0003", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ". In Old Testament Gr. it is sts. used to translate the Hebr. 'ēth (particle prefixed to the definite accus.) through confusion with the Prep. 'ēth 'with',"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ἐμίσησα σὺν τὴν ζωήν LXX Ec. 2.17", "author_abbreviation": "LXX", "tlg_author": "0527", "tlg_work": "030", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; οὐκ ἐμνήσθη ς. τοῦ ἀνδρός ib."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "9.15", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0527", "tlg_work": "030", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ";"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ἔκτισεν ὁ θεὸς σὺν τὸν οὐρανὸν καὶ σὺν τὴν γῆν Aq. Ge. 1.1", "author_abbreviation": "Aq.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", etc. besides, also,"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ς. δὲ πλουτίζειν ἐμέ A. Ag. 586", "author_abbreviation": "A.", "tlg_author": "0085", "tlg_work": "005", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ";"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ς. δ' αὔτως ἐγώ S. Ant. 85", "author_abbreviation": "S.", "tlg_author": "0011", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", etc.;"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ς. δ' ἐγὼ παρών Id. Aj. 1288", "author_abbreviation": "Id.", "tlg_author": "0011", "tlg_work": "003", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", cf."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "El. 299", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0011", "tlg_work": "005", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ";"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Δίρκα τε . . ς. τ' Ἀσωπιάδες κόραι E. HF 785", "author_abbreviation": "E.", "tlg_author": "0006", "tlg_work": "009", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(lyr.); in later Poetry"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ς. καί A.R. 1.74", "author_abbreviation": "A.R.", "tlg_author": "0001", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ","}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Herod. 4.3", "author_abbreviation": "Herod.", "tlg_author": "0650", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ","}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Nic. Th. 8", "author_abbreviation": "Nic.", "tlg_author": "0022", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ","}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "D.P. 843", "author_abbreviation": "D.P.", "tlg_author": "0084", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(also in late Prose,"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Ath. 2.49a", "author_abbreviation": "Ath.", "tlg_author": "0008", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; cf. supr."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "B. 3", "author_abbreviation": "B.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "). IN COMPO"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "S.", "author_abbreviation": "S.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "with, along with, together, at the same time, hence of any kind of union, connexion, or participation in a thing, and metaph. of agreement or unity. In Compos. with a trans. Verb σύν may refer to the Object as well as the Subject, as συγκατακτείνειν may mean kill one person as well as another, or, join with another in killing. of the completion of an action, altogether, completely, as in"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "συνάγνυμι, συνασκέω 2", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", συνθρύπτω, συγκόπτω, συμπατέω, συμπληρόω, συντελέω, συντέμνω; sts., therefore, it seems only to strengthen the force of the simple word. joined with numerals, σύνδυο two together, which sense often becomes distributive, by twos, two and two; so σύντρεις, σύμπεντε, etc., like Lat. bini, terni, etc. σύν in Compos., before β μ π φ ψ, becomes συμ-; before γ κ ξ Χ, συγ-; before λ συλ-; before ς usu. συσ-; but becomes συ- before ς followed by a conson. (e.g. συστῆναι), before ζ, and perh. sts. before ξ. In a poet. passage, ap."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Pl. Phdr. 237a", "author_abbreviation": "Pl.", "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "012", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", we have ξύμ alone in tmesi, ξύμ μοι λάβεσθε for συλλάβεσθέ μοι; cf."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ὅτε ξὺμ πρῶτ' ἐφύοντο Emp. 95", "author_abbreviation": "Emp.", "tlg_author": "1342", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": in Inscrr. and Papyri these assimilations are freq. not found."}]}